Added the ``RSLogix500`` module, which parses Rockwell RSLogix 500 / RSLogix Micro ``.RSS`` project files and backups (SLC 500 and MicroLogix). It extracts and decompresses every stream in the file and decodes the ladder logic of all program files, address descriptions (as tags), rung comments, and processor and project metadata, with limits on size and work so corrupt or crafted files can't exhaust memory or CPU. Files are detected by their contents, so renamed files and backups are found and RSS news feeds are ignored, and the example configuration files now collect ``.RSS`` files with ``peat pillage``.
